          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Oversized Sets</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Large mixed sets always carry sizes you will never use, and the per-tool saving evaporates once you account for the dead weight. Buy the specific ranges you reach for and fill gaps as they appear — Tekton's individual pricing makes that practical.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming a Michigan Address Means Domestic Manufacture</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Tekton engineers, inspects, and distributes from Grand Rapids, and manufactures primarily in Taiwan and China to its own specifications. That is standard across the industry and no reflection on quality, but it is worth knowing before buying on that assumption.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using Chrome Sockets on an Impact Wrench</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Chrome sockets are hand-tool rated and can shatter under impact, which is a genuine safety issue rather than just a durability one. Tekton sells black-oxide impact sockets for that work — the distinction matters more than the brand does.
              </p>
